{\b Ghozt \endash  Dev Tester}\par
\par
This software is provided for use by Capital-Iz and its authorised users.\par
\par
{\b What it does}\par
Ghozt examines software you own or are authorised to test. It registers targets, runs governed sweeps against them, records every observation to an event ledger, captures and hashes evidence, and reports findings with the proof behind them.\par
\par
{\b Authority is yours to establish}\par
Ghozt operates only against targets, environments and actions for which you hold explicit permission. It does not grant that permission and cannot verify it on your behalf. Destructive tests require an access class you set deliberately, and are denied against production by policy. Registering a target is a statement that you are entitled to examine it.\par
\par
{\b Where your data lives}\par
All data stays on this computer, under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Capital-Iz\\Ghozt. Nothing is uploaded anywhere. Evidence artefacts, findings and the event ledger are held in a local database. Uninstalling removes the application but leaves that folder in place, so your evidence survives an upgrade; delete the folder by hand if you want the data gone.\par
\par
{\b Evidence, not assertion}\par
Ghozt records what it observed and marks what it did not. A passing check is evidence of a check that ran, bounded by the scope it was given \endash  it is not a claim that untested scope is sound.\par
\par
{\b No warranty}\par
The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. The authors are not liable for any claim, damages or other liability arising from its use.\par
